[1.221789, "o", "\u001b[1;33m⚠\u001b[0m  --no-human=both runs the implementer AND reviewer phases headless.\r\n   No human is at the keyboard during phase 1 (implementer).\r\n   On a design-fork it cannot safely resolve, the implementer punts the spec\r\n   to Needs Attention instead of guessing — review punts later with `aida findings list`.\r\n   \u001b[2mSet AIDA_NO_HUMAN_ACKNOWLEDGED=1 to skip this prompt on an unattended run,\u001b[0m\r\n   \u001b[2mor `aida no-human acknowledge` once to persist it across runs (per machine; --project to scope to this repo). trace:TASK-394\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n   Continue? [y/N] "]
