[1440.2198, "o", "│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m \u001b[36mBash\u001b[0m: gh pr checks 1293 2>&1 | head -8 || echo \"(checks not yet registered)\"\r\n"]
[1454.733601, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m STORY-744 is shipped to a branch and up for review. Here's the summary:\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m ## STORY-744 — TUI drive verb: honest suitability-gate + clarify/force remedy\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m **The bug:** the redesign TUI drive verb spawned `aida zen <id>` detached with stdio nulled and said \"drive launched\" the instant the child *spawned* — so a gate **hold** (e.g. under-specified) died in the nulled stderr and the operator saw a false positive.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m **What I built** (PR [#1293](https://github.com/joemooney/aida/pull/1293), branch `story-744`, spec → Done):\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m **Slice 1 — honest gate**\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m "]
[1454.733978, "o", "- New `aida zen <spec> --json` gate **probe**: emits the composed eligibility + suitability verdict as JSON *without driving*. The pure `zen_drive::classify_gate` (+ `GateVerdict`) single-sources the *same* classification the drive runs — so the TUI reads the gate rather than parsing human prose.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m - The TUI `Drive` outcome probes first: `ready` → launch as before; a hold → a warn-bordered popup with the reason (no false \"launched\"); an unparseable probe → refuse to vouch.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m **Slice 2 — remedies**\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m - `GateHold` popup: `c` clarify (under-specified), `f` force (soft holds), `Esc`/`q` dismiss.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m - Clarify **suspends** the cockpit (new `term::suspend_for_child`), runs interactive `aida questions clarify <id>` (`/aida-clarify`), then **re-offers** the drive by re-probing.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]"]
[1454.734309, "o", "\u001b[0m - Force → detached `aida zen <id> --force` (soft holds only; hard refusals stay non-overridable).\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m **Key design decision I made:** rather than replicate the gate in the TUI (it can't call aida-cli, and text-parsing stderr is fragile), I added a structured `--json` probe so the classification stays single-sourced in the CLI — the \"substrate as bouncer\" shape. This also gives the follow-up TASK-1075 (full auto-remedy loop) a clean substrate.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m **Verification:** all 6 acceptance criteria covered; new unit tests in both crates (33 + 499 pass); `fmt --check` clean; no new clippy warnings; live-verified the probe (ready / not-eligible / bad-id). CI (Build) is **pending** on the PR.\r\n\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m Per your convention I did **not** auto-merge — it's up for review; merge once the required check is green (`gh pr merge 1293 --squash`). The implementer queue is now empty. The 1 awaiting finding (TASK-1077, a cosmetic doc-comment on PR-1291) is unrelated and still open for triage.\r\n"]
[1454.985086, "o", "\u001b[2m│ [headless:story-744]\u001b[0m ✓ result 1419791ms $13.2253\r\n"]
